  "01 Ledger Verification": "<div class="rounded-[var(--radius-card)] bg-white border border-line p-6 "><div class="p-5"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><div class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5"></path></svg></div><div><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Ledger Verification</h3><div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><span class="rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-blue-50 text-blue-700">ADVISER</span><span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full h-[22px] px-2.5 text-[11px] font-medium whitespace-nowrap bg-[#E6F7F3] text-[#1A7A63] ">Completed</span></div></div></div></div><div class="mb-4 rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-4"><p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1">What to do</p><p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Check each overdue levy was validly raised and its notice served with the hardship information, and that payments were applied to the oldest levies first, then interest, then costs (unless the owner or a court or tribunal order directed otherwise)</p><p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500">Check each overdue levy was validly raised and the levy notice was served with the hardship information. Check payments were applied to the oldest overdue levies first, then interest, then recovery costs, unless the owner or a court or tribunal order said otherwise. Showing levies, interest and costs separately is StrataVerze practice.</p></div><div class="mb-4 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50/50 p-3"><svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-blue-500 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6.042A