  "05 Hardship Review": "<div class="rounded-[var(--radius-card)] bg-white border border-line p-6 "><div class="p-5"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><div class="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-sm font-bold bg-gray-100 text-gray-400">5</div><div><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Hardship Review</h3><div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><span class="rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium bg-purple-50 text-purple-700">COMMITTEE</span><span class="rounded-full bg-amber-50 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-amber-700">Approval Required</span></div></div></div></div><div class="mb-4 rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-4"><p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1">What to do</p><p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Decide any payment plan request (and any request to waive interest) by majority vote at an owners corporation or strata committee meeting, recorded in the minutes, and reply in writing within 28 days. A refusal must give reasons. No fee can be charged. A request can arrive at any step</p><p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-500">A payment plan request (and any request to waive interest) is decided by majority vote at an owners corporation or strata committee meeting and recorded in the minutes. The strata managing agent cannot decide it. Reply in writing within 28 days. A plan can run up to 12 months. A refusal must give reasons; the guidance says a request may be refused if the plan would leave a fund short. No fee can be charged. From 23 Oct 2026 a plan can cover current levies and interest as well as overdue levies. While a plan is followed, no recovery action can be taken for the levies it covers.</p></div><div class="mb-4 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50/50 p-3"><svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-blue-500 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap